WEBVTT

00:02.072 --> 00:03.405
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

00:03.407 --> 00:04.640
Okay.

00:04.642 --> 00:05.974
Hold up your gifts.

00:05.976 --> 00:07.876
Everybody has to see the gold
and frankincense and myrrh

00:07.878 --> 00:09.511
so they know
we're the three wise men.

00:09.513 --> 00:12.080
It's 88 degrees out.

00:12.082 --> 00:13.482
I don't have any myrrh.

00:13.484 --> 00:16.885
Unless it's the biblical term
for “swamp ass.”

00:16.887 --> 00:18.420
We want this
to be mantel-worthy.

00:18.422 --> 00:20.923
We want people to say, you know,
“Look at those costumes,

00:20.925 --> 00:22.991
“look at that view,
look at Cher's house

00:22.993 --> 00:25.527
perfectly positioned
over Alan's right shoulder.”

00:25.529 --> 00:28.130
Oh, it's got to be
better than last year.

00:28.132 --> 00:31.133
Me as Joseph,
Berta as the Virgin Mary

00:31.135 --> 00:33.435
looking down at you in a diaper.

00:33.437 --> 00:35.470
People loved that.

00:35.472 --> 00:37.372
Okay, here we go.

00:38.542 --> 00:40.842
Now everybody say...

00:40.844 --> 00:42.811
Sweet baby Jesus!

00:42.813 --> 00:44.947
Sweet baby Jesus!

00:44.949 --> 00:46.415
Sorry about that.

00:46.417 --> 00:47.683
Oh, that's so cute.

00:47.685 --> 00:49.785
You guys are dressed
as Duck Dynasty.

00:51.155 --> 00:53.555
No. We're the three kings
of Bethlehem.

00:53.557 --> 00:55.157
Oh, right.

00:55.159 --> 00:56.992
I don't get HBO.

00:56.994 --> 00:59.461
Guys, look at him.

00:59.463 --> 01:04.232
Isn't he the cutest
in his little robe and beard?

01:04.234 --> 01:06.001
You want my gold?

01:06.003 --> 01:08.003
Oh!

01:08.005 --> 01:11.239
First cute girl he meets, he's
already giving away his money.

01:12.743 --> 01:15.544
You know, I think I have a
better idea for a holiday card.

01:16.847 --> 01:18.814
♪ Men-men-men, men-men-men ♪

01:18.816 --> 01:21.049
♪ Men-men-men, men-men. ♪

01:21.051 --> 01:22.417
♪ Men, men, men, men ♪

01:22.419 --> 01:23.618
♪ Manly men, men, men ♪

01:23.620 --> 01:25.197
♪ Ah. ♪
♪ Men. ♪

01:25.198 --> 01:29.198
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 12x08 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Clockwise in Back Hole Until Tight&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on December 18, 2014

01:29.199 --> 01:32.199
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

01:32.201 --> 01:33.767
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

01:33.769 --> 01:35.502
I found
the fake snow!

01:35.504 --> 01:37.171
Oh.

01:38.207 --> 01:39.673
It looks real.

01:39.675 --> 01:41.275
Yeah. I love a white Christmas.

01:41.277 --> 01:42.576
So did Charlie.

01:42.578 --> 01:45.179
He used to put snow
on every mirror in the house.

01:45.181 --> 01:47.214
Okay.

01:47.216 --> 01:49.049
Hey, hey, buddy, why
don't you go inside

01:49.051 --> 01:50.651
and write your letter to Santa?

01:50.653 --> 01:52.052
Santa's not real.

01:52.054 --> 01:53.187
What?

01:53.189 --> 01:55.022
Of course he is.

01:55.024 --> 01:57.691
He's never brought me
anything I asked for.

01:57.693 --> 01:59.293
Hey, I am sure

01:59.295 --> 02:01.862
that Santa's gonna come through
for you this year, buddy.

02:01.864 --> 02:04.264
That's what grown-ups
always say.

02:06.135 --> 02:07.868
Come inside with me.

02:07.870 --> 02:11.538
I made gingerbread Zippys.

02:11.540 --> 02:13.707
I was gonna make
gingerbread houses,

02:13.709 --> 02:16.510
but everybody knows
Zippys don't have houses.

02:19.215 --> 02:22.149
A six-year-old boy
who doesn't believe in Santa.

02:22.151 --> 02:24.051
How sad is that?

02:24.053 --> 02:27.187
Almost as sad as my
20-year-old boy who does.

02:27.189 --> 02:28.755
This sucks.

02:28.757 --> 02:31.391
Just 'cause he grew up
in a group home doesn't mean

02:31.393 --> 02:33.427
that he can't enjoy
the magic of Christmas.

02:33.429 --> 02:35.762
I know. It was always
Jake's favorite holiday.

02:35.764 --> 02:37.164
Especially the year he turned 13

02:37.166 --> 02:39.266
and got his first
Christmas boner.

02:40.402 --> 02:43.036
It was the only toy
he played with all day.

02:43.038 --> 02:45.572
Hey, you know,
I bet Louis would believe

02:45.574 --> 02:47.708
if we got him
exactly what he wanted.

02:47.710 --> 02:49.309
I don't know what he wants.

02:49.311 --> 02:50.577
He wants a bike.

02:50.579 --> 02:52.579
God! Rose.

02:52.581 --> 02:54.715
What are you
doing here?

02:54.717 --> 02:56.283
Wait. How do you know
about Louis?

02:56.285 --> 02:59.086
Oh, Walden, you're so adorable.

02:59.088 --> 03:01.755
I just wanted to bring by
my homemade Christmas candies.

03:01.757 --> 03:03.624
Do you like nuts?

03:04.960 --> 03:07.661
Covered in chocolate, yes.

03:07.663 --> 03:09.663
With a sweater and skirt, no.

03:09.665 --> 03:11.598
Oh. Okay.

03:11.600 --> 03:14.801
On this day, Walden's heart
shrank three sizes.

03:14.803 --> 03:16.236
Anyway,

03:16.238 --> 03:18.305
I know this time of year
can get busy,

03:18.307 --> 03:20.407
so if you need a helping hand,
I'm here.

03:20.409 --> 03:23.577
I can wrap presents or babysit
or read a Christmas story.

03:23.579 --> 03:25.279
I'm great at doing voices.

03:25.281 --> 03:27.548
Or hearing them.

03:27.550 --> 03:29.116
What do you want, Rose?

03:29.118 --> 03:31.818
My DNA, my fingerprints,
a lock of my hair?

03:31.820 --> 03:33.420
No, silly.

03:33.422 --> 03:35.322
I have all that.

03:35.324 --> 03:36.790
I want to be your friend again.

03:36.792 --> 03:38.492
I don't think
that I'm comfortable

03:38.494 --> 03:40.227
with you being around Louis.

03:40.229 --> 03:42.095
Or me.

03:42.097 --> 03:44.698
If you want to hang out
with Alan, that's fine.

03:45.935 --> 03:48.135
I'll pass.

03:49.305 --> 03:51.271
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

03:51.273 --> 03:55.175
Here you go-- a little
Christmas cheer for everyone.

03:55.177 --> 03:58.445
Ugh! What is this?

03:58.447 --> 03:59.379
It's eggnog.

03:59.381 --> 04:01.114
With no rum!

04:02.218 --> 04:04.885
Eggnog without booze
is as boring and bland

04:04.887 --> 04:07.054
as church without booze.

04:09.091 --> 04:12.926
Be a dear and go get some
rum for your grandmother.

04:12.928 --> 04:16.163
Evelyn, he's six years old.

04:16.165 --> 04:18.765
Oh. Yes, right.

04:18.767 --> 04:22.669
The rum is in a bottle
with a pirate on it.

04:22.671 --> 04:26.440
Maybe-maybe we can wait
until Louis goes to bed.

04:26.442 --> 04:28.242
Of course.

04:28.244 --> 04:29.943
So run along to bed, dear.

04:29.945 --> 04:31.211
Mom.

04:31.213 --> 04:33.580
If you don't go to sleep,
Santa won't come.

04:33.582 --> 04:34.648
There is no Santa.

04:34.650 --> 04:36.717
What?! Of course there is.

04:36.719 --> 04:39.319
Santa's as real
as the nose on my face.

04:40.556 --> 04:44.524
Well, he's as real as my...

04:46.495 --> 04:48.662
Trust me, he's real.

04:48.664 --> 04:52.699
You know, she's right, and
tonight we're gonna prove it,

04:52.701 --> 04:56.370
because we got
a Santa cam,

04:56.372 --> 05:00.374
so we can catch
the big man in red on video.

05:00.376 --> 05:02.175
Santa Claus!

05:02.177 --> 05:03.543
Old Saint Nick!

05:03.545 --> 05:05.479
Papa Noel.

05:05.481 --> 05:07.547
Babbo Natale.

05:07.549 --> 05:09.716
Weihnachtsmann.

05:10.886 --> 05:14.288
Which, of course,
means “Christmas man” in German.

05:14.290 --> 05:16.256
Teachable moment.

05:16.258 --> 05:18.358
The-the point is,
in the morning,

05:18.360 --> 05:20.260
when you see
him on video,

05:20.262 --> 05:22.195
then you'll believe
he's real, right?

05:22.197 --> 05:23.263
I guess.

05:23.265 --> 05:26.166
I guess?! What?

05:26.168 --> 05:27.401
It's a Christmas miracle!

05:27.403 --> 05:29.436
Did you hear that, Alan?
Did you hear that, Evelyn?

05:29.438 --> 05:30.837
You hear that, Clarence?

05:30.839 --> 05:33.206
Merry Christmas, you wonderful
old building and loan!

05:33.208 --> 05:36.677
Okay, off to bed you go.

05:36.679 --> 05:39.313
And soon, you'll have
visions of sugar plums

05:39.315 --> 05:41.248
dancing in your head.

05:41.250 --> 05:43.684
Can I have some pirate rum?

05:43.686 --> 05:45.619
No, we don't want visions

05:45.621 --> 05:48.288
of pink elephants
dancing in our head.

05:48.290 --> 05:52.526
Okay, you go brush your teeth,
and I'll be in in a minute.

05:52.528 --> 05:54.328
When Alan was little
and couldn't sleep,

05:54.330 --> 05:55.862
I used to give him whiskey.

05:55.864 --> 05:58.865
Breast-feeding
doesn't count, Mother.

05:58.867 --> 06:01.468
So here's the plan.

06:01.470 --> 06:03.537
Santa's not actually coming.

06:03.539 --> 06:05.272
You don't say.

06:05.274 --> 06:06.673
But how awesome is this?

06:06.675 --> 06:09.843
We got the number two guy from
the Thanksgiving Day Parade.

06:09.845 --> 06:11.411
So, if the giant

06:11.413 --> 06:14.014
Bullwinkle balloon breaks loose
and kills the number one Santa,

06:14.016 --> 06:15.415
this is the guy.

06:15.417 --> 06:16.750
Yeah.

06:16.752 --> 06:18.218
He also appeared as Santa

06:18.220 --> 06:20.721
on an episode of
&lt;i>Walker, Texas Ranger.&lt;/i>

06:22.491 --> 06:26.893
He and Chuck Norris fought the
bad guys with Christmas fu.

06:28.130 --> 06:29.996
So, when he gets here,
he's gonna take the presents

06:29.998 --> 06:32.232
that we bought for him, and he's
gonna put them under the tree,

06:32.234 --> 06:33.900
and then we'll get it on video,

06:33.902 --> 06:37.604
and then Louis will have the
perfect Charlie Brown Christmas.

06:37.606 --> 06:40.140
♪ Lou, Lou, Lou ♪

06:40.142 --> 06:42.209
♪ Lou-Lou, Lou, Lou, Lou ♪

06:42.211 --> 06:43.744
♪ Lou, Lou, Lou ♪

06:43.746 --> 06:45.712
♪ Lou-Lou, Lou, Lou ♪

06:45.714 --> 06:49.516
♪ Lou, Lou, Lou,
Lou-Lou, Lou, Lou, Lou... ♪

06:49.518 --> 06:50.617
I need rum.

06:50.619 --> 06:51.852
♪ Lou, Lou, Lou ♪

06:51.854 --> 06:53.320
♪ Lou, Lou, Lou, Lou... ♪

06:53.322 --> 06:54.921
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

06:54.923 --> 06:56.456
Santa's here!

06:56.458 --> 06:59.326
I give you
Kris Kringle.

07:01.964 --> 07:03.130
Are you smoking pot?

07:03.132 --> 07:04.931
Of course not.

07:06.402 --> 07:07.734
Don't worry.

07:07.736 --> 07:09.669
Santa's got a prescription card.

07:09.671 --> 07:11.638
Well, apparently, the presents

07:11.640 --> 07:13.707
have already been
delivered in Colorado.

07:14.943 --> 07:17.144
Here. Come on in.

07:19.148 --> 07:22.249
I'm Walden.
This is Alan and, uh, Evelyn.

07:22.251 --> 07:24.718
Uh, wh-what do you go by?
Mr. Claus?

07:25.921 --> 07:28.054
Babbo Natale?

07:29.291 --> 07:31.057
Weihnachtsmann?

07:31.059 --> 07:33.260
Actually, it's Frank.

07:33.262 --> 07:35.362
It's not very Christmasy.

07:35.364 --> 07:36.696
Well, if you don't like it,

07:36.698 --> 07:39.833
I can hang some mistletoe
over my ass.

07:40.769 --> 07:43.570
That's my son
you're talking to.

07:44.373 --> 07:45.373
Good one.

07:46.642 --> 07:48.909
I-I... I'm sorry.
We're-we're just really excited.

07:48.911 --> 07:51.178
It's our first Christmas
with our foster son.

07:51.180 --> 07:53.280
Uh, basically,
what we're gonna do is

07:53.282 --> 07:55.515
film you putting the presents
under the tree.

07:55.517 --> 07:57.784
Uh, and then I've written
a little something

07:57.786 --> 07:59.252
for you to say to Louis.

07:59.254 --> 08:00.454
Let me guess.

08:00.456 --> 08:04.157
“Ho, ho, ho!
Merry Christmas, Louis!”

08:04.159 --> 08:05.926
Oh, that's better.

08:05.928 --> 08:06.993
Go with that.

08:06.995 --> 08:08.495
Okay, okay, okay,
and then...

08:08.497 --> 08:10.897
then you'll take a
bite of the cookie,

08:10.899 --> 08:14.100
you'll crunch the carrot,
you'll sip the milk,

08:14.102 --> 08:17.037
wink at the camera, jiggle
your belly and leave.

08:17.973 --> 08:19.873
So it's toys,
bite, crunch,

08:19.875 --> 08:22.008
sip, wink,
jiggle, leave.

08:23.278 --> 08:25.445
Toys, bite, crunch, sip,
wink, jiggle, leave.

08:26.448 --> 08:27.280
Got it?

08:27.282 --> 08:29.583
So you want me to be Santa.

08:29.585 --> 08:33.353
Toys, bite, crunch, sip,
wink, jiggle, leave.

08:33.355 --> 08:36.656
That sounds a lot like an orgy
I had in Palm Springs once.

08:36.658 --> 08:39.659
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

08:39.661 --> 08:42.128
All right,
let's get this stuff wrapped

08:42.130 --> 08:45.165
so we can enjoy this holiday
the way I always imagined.

08:45.167 --> 08:49.169
Listening to Michael Bublé's
Christmas album...

08:49.171 --> 08:51.505
with my husband.

08:51.507 --> 08:54.841
Aw, looks like Alan's getting
his first gift early.

08:54.843 --> 08:57.811
Where's the boy's bike?

08:57.813 --> 08:59.946
Oh, right here.

09:01.583 --> 09:03.917
That's not a boy's bike.
That's a box.

09:05.420 --> 09:06.720
The boy's bike's in the box.

09:06.722 --> 09:09.656
Tell me the boy's bike
in the box has been built.

09:09.658 --> 09:12.225
Oh, no, they wanted $75
to assemble it.

09:13.495 --> 09:15.161
That's like ten pairs of pants.

09:15.163 --> 09:17.797
I was paying for it!

09:17.799 --> 09:19.966
Oh, come on.

09:19.968 --> 09:22.135
How hard could it be?

09:24.439 --> 09:26.373
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

09:26.375 --> 09:28.108
Uh, sorry, looks like
it's gonna be

09:28.110 --> 09:29.543
a little longer
than we expected.

09:29.545 --> 09:32.178
Uh, any chance you know how
to put together a bike?

09:32.180 --> 09:36.516
Right now, I'm too buzzed
to have a tool in my hand.

09:37.786 --> 09:40.854
I'm just buzzed enough
to have a tool in mine.

09:42.691 --> 09:44.958
Well, ho, ho, ho.

09:44.960 --> 09:46.626
Exactly.

09:46.628 --> 09:48.128
Here.

09:48.130 --> 09:51.565
Let me get us both
a little more eggnog.

09:51.567 --> 09:55.635
Um, Santa, did you drive your
own sleigh over here tonight?

09:55.637 --> 09:58.538
Nope. Santa Ubered.

10:00.275 --> 10:03.343
Oh, well, uh, hope your driver
was named Rudolph.

10:04.947 --> 10:06.746
Um, so what's going on?

10:06.748 --> 10:07.981
Does Santa know you're married?

10:07.983 --> 10:11.885
Does the IRS know
you don't have five children?

10:13.689 --> 10:16.122
Marty and I have
an open marriage.

10:16.124 --> 10:17.657
And since he's 93,

10:17.659 --> 10:21.127
my end opens a little more
frequently than his.

10:21.129 --> 10:23.296
As does your mouth.

10:23.298 --> 10:27.534
That's one of the ends
I was talking about.

10:29.538 --> 10:31.237
Here you go.

10:31.239 --> 10:34.975
You're running low on eggnog,
so this one is all rum.

10:34.977 --> 10:37.077
Thank you.

10:37.079 --> 10:39.079
You know, this is a situation

10:39.081 --> 10:41.481
where Santa doesn't
need a little helper.

10:43.018 --> 10:45.652
So on, Prancer.

10:45.654 --> 10:47.354
Fine.

10:47.356 --> 10:48.822
But just know this:

10:48.824 --> 10:52.258
I am not afraid to give Santa
a negative review on Yelp.

10:53.261 --> 10:55.362
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

10:55.364 --> 10:58.331
Okay, I can't make heads
or tails of these instructions.

10:58.333 --> 10:59.733
They're barely in English.

10:59.735 --> 11:02.202
Uh, “The bolts of turning

11:02.204 --> 11:05.939
“shall revolve clockwords

11:05.941 --> 11:09.709
as in above figure below.”

11:09.711 --> 11:13.413
Does it say anything about
roommate of cheapness shall have

11:13.415 --> 11:16.583
foot inserted
in back hole till tight?

11:16.585 --> 11:18.018
Oh.

11:18.020 --> 11:19.919
I guess on the first day
of Christmas,

11:19.921 --> 11:21.688
my true love threatened me.

11:21.690 --> 11:23.423
I'm sorry, but it's Louis's

11:23.425 --> 11:24.958
first Christmas
not in the group home,

11:24.960 --> 11:26.760
and I want it to be perfect.

11:26.762 --> 11:28.662
No Christmas is ever perfect.

11:28.664 --> 11:29.896
There's always gonna be a toy

11:29.898 --> 11:31.931
that's broken
or the wrong kind of batteries.

11:31.933 --> 11:33.633
I mean, even on
the very first Christmas,

11:33.635 --> 11:36.970
Mary and Joseph woke up
to the smell of donkey crap.

11:36.972 --> 11:39.339
I know. I just...

11:39.341 --> 11:41.307
I want him to believe in Santa,

11:41.309 --> 11:42.909
and-and get this bike

11:42.911 --> 11:46.146
and-and wake up to a
winter wonderland.

11:46.148 --> 11:48.748
Not that I ordered
a truckload of snow.

11:49.885 --> 11:51.951
I didn't get reindeer!

11:51.953 --> 11:54.421
Well, they're endangered.

11:54.423 --> 11:57.290
We could still make
Christmas special for Louis.

11:57.292 --> 11:59.492
We just got to finish this bike.
We can do this.

11:59.494 --> 12:02.462
You're right. We got
an M.I.T. engineer and a...

12:02.464 --> 12:04.864
formerly board-certified
chiropractor.

12:04.866 --> 12:06.800
Yeah, now we're talking.

12:06.802 --> 12:08.301
I mean, this can't
be more difficult

12:08.303 --> 12:10.070
than realigning someone's spine.

12:10.072 --> 12:12.205
Here.
You know, you got, uh...

12:12.207 --> 12:15.241
you got your, uh, your L2,
uh, connected to your L3.

12:15.243 --> 12:17.343
And all we have to do is

12:17.345 --> 12:20.547
put the right pressure
on the right spot and...

12:23.885 --> 12:26.319
Uh, and that is why I am

12:26.321 --> 12:30.256
a&lt;i> formerly&lt;/i> board-certified
chiropractor.

12:30.258 --> 12:31.691
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

12:34.429 --> 12:37.363
Oh, Santa.

12:39.901 --> 12:42.068
Oh, Santa!

12:43.705 --> 12:45.572
Oh, no.

12:46.808 --> 12:49.843
Here comes Santa Claus!

12:49.845 --> 12:53.613
Here comes
Santa Claus!

12:53.615 --> 12:56.082
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

13:02.513 --> 13:04.713
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

13:04.715 --> 13:06.115
Oh, my God.

13:06.117 --> 13:07.282
What happened?

13:07.284 --> 13:09.318
I saw Mommy banging Santa Claus.

13:10.921 --> 13:14.323
What?
It's 1972 all over again.

13:15.459 --> 13:17.426
We have a problem.

13:17.428 --> 13:19.128
Yes, you have a problem.

13:19.130 --> 13:22.231
You are the Christmas whore!

13:22.233 --> 13:25.868
Be that as it may, I think
I killed Santa Claus.

13:25.870 --> 13:28.404
Oh, God!

13:28.406 --> 13:30.606
It's exactly like 1972!

13:32.109 --> 13:34.076
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

13:34.078 --> 13:35.411
Is he gonna be okay?

13:35.413 --> 13:37.012
Yeah, It was just
atrial fibrillation.

13:37.014 --> 13:39.148
He just needs some medication
and a few days rest.

13:39.150 --> 13:42.584
You hear that, sweetheart?
I'll be fine by New Year's.

13:42.586 --> 13:45.387
I'll be counting down
till the balls drop.

13:48.292 --> 13:50.492
Well, thank God Louis
didn't see any of this.

13:50.494 --> 13:52.027
He would've been
traumatized.

13:52.029 --> 13:54.363
Louis? What about me?

13:54.365 --> 13:57.366
The man almost died
while he was having sex with me.

13:58.235 --> 14:00.502
That's not easy to get over.

14:00.504 --> 14:03.739
No matter how many times
it happens.

14:04.708 --> 14:07.009
Okay, well, all right,
well, there you have it.

14:07.011 --> 14:08.877
Merry Christmas, Louis.

14:08.879 --> 14:12.648
Your grandmother banged Santa
within an inch of his life.

14:12.650 --> 14:15.417
Here's half a bike!

14:15.419 --> 14:16.585
W-We can salvage this.

14:16.587 --> 14:18.754
There's still enough time
to-to finish the bike,

14:18.756 --> 14:20.956
wrap the other gifts
and get them under the tree.

14:20.958 --> 14:22.925
Okay, you're right.

14:22.927 --> 14:25.961
Louis will be asleep
for six more hours.

14:25.963 --> 14:27.663
Walden?

14:27.665 --> 14:29.898
Oh, come on!

14:29.900 --> 14:32.301
I heard a noise. Did Santa come?

14:32.303 --> 14:33.969
Sadly, no.

14:35.539 --> 14:38.340
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

14:38.342 --> 14:40.375
All right.

14:40.377 --> 14:41.743
Where's Evelyn?

14:41.745 --> 14:44.012
Oh, well, uh...

14:44.014 --> 14:47.082
she went to her house
to play with...

14:47.084 --> 14:48.350
her toys.

14:48.352 --> 14:50.285
All right, time for bed, bud.

14:50.287 --> 14:52.454
That's right. Santa's on his way.
All right.

14:52.456 --> 14:53.889
If Santa is real,

14:53.891 --> 14:56.692
then how does he get in all
the kids' houses in one night?

14:56.694 --> 15:00.062
Well, he's got
Christmas magic.

15:00.064 --> 15:02.531
And how does he know
where everybody lives?

15:02.533 --> 15:06.568
Well... that's the magic
of Google Maps.

15:06.570 --> 15:08.237
All right.

15:08.239 --> 15:10.806
Good night, buddy.
Time to go to sleep.

15:10.808 --> 15:13.442
Can you guys stay with me
till I fall asleep?

15:14.645 --> 15:16.712
Sure.
Yeah.

15:16.714 --> 15:20.682
It's not like we need to help
Santa assemble toys.

15:21.752 --> 15:25.087
He pays his elves
$75 to do that.

15:26.891 --> 15:28.824
That's Timothy's spot.

15:28.826 --> 15:30.425
Oh, oh, okay.

15:30.427 --> 15:31.493
Um...

15:31.495 --> 15:33.662
I guess, uh...

15:44.141 --> 15:45.908
Good boy.

15:47.611 --> 15:49.912
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

15:53.717 --> 15:55.150
Alan?

15:55.152 --> 15:56.618
Mm-hmm?

15:58.055 --> 15:59.721
Oh, oh, my God!

15:59.723 --> 16:01.189
Oh, don't flatter yourself.

16:01.191 --> 16:03.625
I get one every morning.

16:03.627 --> 16:05.093
Where's Louis?

16:05.095 --> 16:06.194
Hmm?

16:06.196 --> 16:07.629
It's 7:00.
We fell asleep.

16:07.631 --> 16:09.364
Oh, crap. Th-The bike.

16:09.366 --> 16:11.066
The presents.
What are we gonna do?

16:11.068 --> 16:14.169
Well, is it too late to
tell him we're Jewish?

16:15.806 --> 16:17.839
What the...

16:17.841 --> 16:20.142
Santa came! He is real!

16:20.144 --> 16:21.510
Did you...?

16:21.512 --> 16:22.778
No.

16:22.780 --> 16:24.713
He's on the video.

16:26.216 --> 16:31.520
You didn't see Grandma Evelyn
wrestling with Santa, did you?

16:31.522 --> 16:34.056
No, just Santa.

16:34.058 --> 16:36.158
That's...

16:36.160 --> 16:38.627
Santa.

16:38.629 --> 16:39.962
Oh, my God.

16:39.964 --> 16:42.197
If the Easy Bake Oven
I have always wanted

16:42.199 --> 16:45.434
is under that tree,
it is gonna blow my mind.

16:45.436 --> 16:47.436
Can I go outside
and ride my bike?

16:47.438 --> 16:49.471
Sure.

16:49.473 --> 16:51.073
Alan, do you
want to...?

16:51.075 --> 16:52.374
Oh, yeah. Absolutely.

16:52.376 --> 16:54.710
Uh, let's go, buddy.

16:54.712 --> 16:56.712
Looks like we had
a great Christmas

16:56.714 --> 16:58.880
and saved $75.

17:14.665 --> 17:17.132
Rose?

17:17.134 --> 17:19.501
All right, come on, Rose,
I know you're down there.

17:19.503 --> 17:20.702
Actually, I'm
behind you.

17:20.704 --> 17:22.137
Ah, son of a...!

17:22.139 --> 17:24.740
How do you do that?

17:24.742 --> 17:26.408
&lt;i>Why&lt;/i> do you do that?!

17:26.410 --> 17:29.144
Oh, a girl's got to have
a little fun.

17:29.146 --> 17:30.946
Merry Christmas.

17:30.948 --> 17:34.016
I-I cannot believe that you
went to all that trouble for us.

17:34.018 --> 17:37.352
You mean you can't believe
Santa went to all that trouble.

17:37.354 --> 17:39.521
Okay, then I guess

17:39.523 --> 17:42.491
I need to say
thank you to Santa.

17:42.493 --> 17:44.526
Well, he doesn't
do it for the thanks,

17:44.528 --> 17:46.128
he does it because
he genuinely wants

17:46.130 --> 17:48.463
to make the people
in his life happy.

17:49.400 --> 17:50.899
Are you happy, Walden?

17:50.901 --> 17:52.467
I am.

17:52.469 --> 17:55.570
I-I couldn't have imagined
a better Christmas morning.

17:55.572 --> 17:59.474
I mean, other than waking up
with Alan poking me in the back.

17:59.476 --> 18:01.777
Listen, I...

18:01.779 --> 18:05.414
I'm sorry that I said
I didn't want you around.

18:05.416 --> 18:06.715
Oh, please.

18:06.717 --> 18:08.316
It's not like every time
somebody says

18:08.318 --> 18:10.919
something mean to me, I write
it down in a big book called

18:10.921 --> 18:13.588
“Those Who Have Wronged Me.”

18:13.590 --> 18:15.557
That's funny.

18:15.559 --> 18:16.992
I think.

18:16.994 --> 18:21.697
Well, I told you before,
I just want to be your friend.

18:21.699 --> 18:23.665
Well, you are.

18:23.667 --> 18:25.534
And...

18:25.536 --> 18:27.436
I'm sorry if I forgot that.

18:27.438 --> 18:29.204
Oh.

18:31.008 --> 18:32.974
Oh, hey, but how did Santa

18:32.976 --> 18:35.010
manage to put
that bike together?

18:35.012 --> 18:37.946
The instructions couldn't
have been any clearer.

18:37.948 --> 18:40.215
“The bolts of turning
shall revolve clockwords

18:40.217 --> 18:41.850
as in above figure below.”

18:41.852 --> 18:44.186
Duh.

18:44.188 --> 18:47.823
Yeah. Duh.

18:47.825 --> 18:50.092
Do you guys have
big plans for later?

18:50.094 --> 18:52.060
Uh, no, just the usual.

18:52.062 --> 18:54.329
Open gifts, call family,

18:54.331 --> 18:56.364
hope that you get
their voice mail.

18:56.366 --> 18:58.700
Oh, the best part is
Alan's gonna deep-fry a turkey,

18:58.702 --> 19:01.570
so there's a 50/50 chance
he'll catch himself on fire.

19:01.572 --> 19:03.405
Oh, I got you guys

19:03.407 --> 19:06.441
a little something
for the house.

19:06.443 --> 19:08.243
And I hope that every time
you look at it,

19:08.245 --> 19:09.444
you'll think of me.

19:11.215 --> 19:13.915
Oh! A cuckoo clock.

19:13.917 --> 19:15.684
I get it. 'Cause you're...

19:17.721 --> 19:19.121
What?

19:20.190 --> 19:22.190
No.

19:22.192 --> 19:24.593
Because it's red like a rose.

19:25.562 --> 19:27.462
How could you
hurt me on Christmas?

19:27.464 --> 19:29.297
I'm sorry. I-I...

19:29.299 --> 19:31.333
I thought it was...
Oh, I'm just kidding.

19:31.335 --> 19:34.503
No, it's totally
'cause I'm cuckoo.

19:35.272 --> 19:37.973
Well, Merry Christmas, Walden.

19:41.745 --> 19:43.945
Merry Christmas, Rose.

19:49.253 --> 19:52.521
How cute is that?
It's a tiny Rose.

19:52.523 --> 19:55.824
Wait, is that her real hair?

19:55.826 --> 19:57.726
No, it's yours.

19:57.728 --> 19:59.828
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:05.229 --> 20:08.763
♪ You better watch out,
you better not cry ♪

20:08.764 --> 20:10.831
♪ You better not pout... ♪
You know,

20:10.833 --> 20:13.700
this is what Christmas
is all about.

20:13.702 --> 20:17.104
Family, Bublé,

20:17.106 --> 20:20.107
deep-fried turkey.

20:20.109 --> 20:21.809
Life is good, Alan.

20:21.811 --> 20:24.011
Hmm. It is.

20:31.320 --> 20:33.320
Um, can you cut mine for me?

20:33.322 --> 20:35.522
Deep-fried fingers.

20:44.066 --> 20:45.899
That was sweet of Rose.
Yeah.

20:45.901 --> 20:48.268
You know, I-I've always
been so cynical of her.

20:48.270 --> 20:50.871
Maybe she does just want
to be friends, you know?

20:50.873 --> 20:55.669
♪ Now, he sees you
when you're sleeping... ♪

20:57.300 --> 21:03.800
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>
